      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A historic rainy season, a deluge of historic proportions, triggered a cascade of engineered releases and natural runoff that overcame the Euphrates' defenses. The surge inundated settlements and agricultural lands in Deir Ezzor and Raqqa, claiming the innocent lives lost among children. The state's operational arm deployed boats for evacuations, while the head of state appeared at the disaster site, and the source of the upstream pressure was pressured into concessions to lower discharges.",
